            "type": "paragraph",
            "value": "This fractured architecture induces a severe operational failure mode known as 'phantom inventory': stock discrepancies between the central ERP ledger (such as SAP S/4HANA or Oracle Retail) and real-time shelf availability. In typical Indian retail operations, batch synchronization between warehouse management systems (WMS) and e-commerce storefronts runs on periodic 15-to-60-minute cron cycles. During peak Indian festive sales (such as Diwali, Dussehra, and Independence Day promotions) or sudden quick-commerce surges, this latency leads to major double-selling, cancellation penalties, and out-of-stock rates exceeding 14.2%. Simultaneously, slow-moving SKUs languish in peripheral stores without dynamic markdown automation, inflating holding costs and trapping crores in illiquid working capital."
