            "type": "paragraph",
            "value": "The Open Network for Digital Commerce (ONDC) has emerged as the definitive national protocol democratizing Indian digital retail. Under the Beckn Protocol specification (v1.2.0), seller platforms must expose standardized, low-latency API contracts to handle `search`, `select`, `init`, `confirm`, `status`, and `track` callbacks. When hundreds of Buyer Applications (such as Paytm, Magicpin, Pincode by PhonePe, and Ola) query a seller network simultaneously, retail backend systems face immense read amplification."
