            "type": "paragraph",
            "value": "LayoutLMv3 integrates three distinct embedding streams:\n1. **Text Token Embeddings:** The textual content is tokenized using Byte-Pair Encoding (BPE), capturing the lexical meaning of words and characters.\n2. **2D Spatial Layout Embeddings:** For every word, a normalized bounding box `[x0, y0, x1, y1]` is computed relative to the document page dimensions (scaled from 0 to 1,000). Spatial position embeddings encode horizontal and vertical distance vectors, allowing the attention heads to associate floating keys (such as 'HSN/SAC Code' or 'Invoice Total') with their corresponding numeric values regardless of column width.\n3. **Visual Patch Embeddings:** The page image is partitioned into uniform visual patches (e.g., 16x16 pixels) and projected linearly through a Vision Transformer (ViT) backbone. Visual embeddings capture non-textual structural indicators: table grid borders, signature lines, corporate letterhead logos, and official government stamp seals."
