            "type": "paragraph",
            "value": "Under Section 8(4) and Section 9 of India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023, data fiduciaries face statutory penalties of up to \u20b9250 Crore for failing to institute reasonable security safeguards against personal data breaches. When consumer data traverses third-party low-code SaaS providers, enterprise legal teams lose control over log persistence, cross-border token replication, and third-party sub-processors."
